//api.github.com/users/Rindbee/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-13T15:29:19Z","updated_at":"2025-01-13T15:30:39Z","body":"@MJacred Things are more complicated than I initially thought. Especially in the case of being between the minimum removal index and the maximum removal index.  For example, suppose that more than three indexes are removed, and there is another guid between the minimum removed index and the maximum removed index, and the guid has multiple mipping records.\r\n```\r\n--------r0--ai-----r1-aj---r2----r3------\r\n```\r\n\r\nUsing simple variables is not enough to record these shifts. To do this, we may need to record all of the mapping indexes of the `p_guid`.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2587435031/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2587445262","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98792#issuecomment-2587445262","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98792","id":2587445262,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6aOUgO","user":{"login":"MJacred","id":6639237,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2MzkyMzc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6639237?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred","html_url":"https://github.com/MJacred","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-13T15:33:08Z","updated_at":"2025-01-13T15:53:04Z","body":"@Rindbee: I think I got it.\r\n\r\nAlternatively, I can iterate over `joy_names` in the first for-loop, right where I remove the entry and fix the offset for each affected joypad right then and there\r\n\r\n**EDIT**: fixed syntax check failure and typo\r\n\r\n**EDIT 2**: did a comparison with original commit, and the differences are\r\n* early exit if nothing removed\r\n* use `fallback_mapping` instead of setting to `-1` for joypads that used this guid and which was not the fallback mapping\r\n* simplified joypad mapping fix `if (count == 1)` (which should be the case 99% of the time)\r\n  * else, the old inner-loop is back again\r\n* 2 new helper variables allowing the early exit and skipping unnecessary mapping fixings","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2587445262/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2598729465","html_url":